course: dictionary
lesson: 3159
title: Leaving home for good
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Emigration is leaving your own country to go and live in another country permanently. The key word is permanently. A holiday or a short visit is not emigration, because you plan to come back. «A visit can become an emigration» only when the visitor decides to stay abroad for good.
explain: Geography and history lessons use emigration to explain why people moved. Push factors push people out of a place, such as no work or danger at home. Pull factors draw people to a new place, such as jobs or family already living there. «Mass emigration» means very many people leaving together.
explain: Use the clues in a sentence. «A wave of emigration from Britain sent many families across the ocean.» The words wave and many show that a large number of people left. The word emigration names the leaving, and a person who leaves is an emigrant.
fact: Emigration means leaving your own country to live permanently in another country.
fact: A person who emigrates is called an emigrant.
fact: Push factors push people out of a country, such as a lack of work or danger; pull factors draw them to a new country, such as jobs or family.
fact: «Mass emigration» means many people leaving at once; «emigration from» tells you the place people left.
fact: Many people made emigration from Ireland and Britain to the USA, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: What does emigration mean? | Moving house within the same town | Going on a week-long visit to see family abroad | Coming home after a long trip | *Leaving your own country to live permanently in another country
exercise: A family leaves their village because there is no work and it is not safe there. Is this a push factor or a pull factor? | A holiday | *A push factor | A pull factor | A museum visit
exercise: «The mass emigration from the village left only a few families behind.» What does mass mean here? | Very few people | A type of church | Something made of metal | *Very many people, all at once
test: Sam's grandmother left Scotland to live in Canada for good. What is this? | A short visit | A day at the beach | *Emigration | A school trip
test: Many families made emigration from Britain to which country in the past? | *Australia | The same country they came from | Under the sea | Their own town
exam: Ella is going to Canada for two weeks and then flying home. Is this emigration? | Yes, because Canada is far away | Yes, she is leaving her country | Yes, because she is going abroad | *No, she plans to come back
